$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=korselt  LOC_AFTER=?

* Korselt's criterion, sufficiency: a squarefree N such that ( q - 1 )
  divides ( N - 1 ) for every prime q dividing N satisfies
  a ^ N == a mod N for every integer a. (The Carmichael property, with
  compositeness stated separately.)

1::simpll1  |- ( ( ( ( N e. NN /\ ( mmu ` N ) =/= 0 /\ A. p e. Prime ( p || N -> ( p - 1 ) || ( N - 1 ) ) ) /\ a e. ZZ ) /\ q e. Prime ) -> N e. NN )
